  "body": "I'd like to propose using `.mjs` more consistently in module specifier examples, to more clearly separate modules from classic scripts.\n\nIn practice, Node.js requires `.mjs` for modules, and on the web file extensions doesn't matter. On top of any host environment requirements, there is value in clearly making the distinction between modules and classic scripts during development. Dedicated file extensions for each type of script accomplish this. Thus, the most pragmatic (and in my opinion, the most WHATWG-like) solution nowadays is to use `.mjs` for modules consistently regardless of the platform.\n\nThis patch intentionally leaves in some module specifier examples ending with `.js`, `.cgi`, or no extension at all (to match the reality of the web, where file extensions don't matter, but HTTP headers do). It just uses `.mjs` by default in examples involving modules.\n\nWhat do you think?\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3810/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 9, 2018, 6:51 AM GMT (cbcd0fb)\">/links.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3810/5a6930a...cbcd0fb/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 9, 2018, 6:51 AM GMT (cbcd0fb)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3810/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 9, 2018, 6:51 AM GMT (cbcd0fb)\">/scripting.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3810/5a6930a...cbcd0fb/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 9, 2018, 6:51 AM GMT (cbcd0fb)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3810/webappapis.html\" title=\"L